  "body": "On main `717ce0a807ea4c6b540d015b5c408723175b2838`, fractional steps below one make `eachHourOfInterval` loop without advancing the date:\n\n```ts\neachHourOfInterval(\n  { start: new Date(\"2024-01-01T00:00:00Z\"), end: new Date(\"2024-01-01T03:00:00Z\") },\n  { step: 0.5 },\n);\n```\n\n`Date.setHours(date.getHours() + step)` discards the fraction. The next iteration therefore appends the same date again. `-0.5` has the same problem after the sign is removed.\n\nThe Temporal implementation instead throws `RangeError` for fractional steps, including `1.5`, which the Date implementation treats as a one-hour step.\n\nReproduced against the actual source with Node 26.10.0 and `TZ=UTC`. A separate child process times out for both sub-hour steps; the integer-step control exits normally. Four added cases fail in the existing Temporal suite, while its 21 existing cases pass.\n\nTruncating the step before checking for zero and handling its sign would avoid the loop and give both implementations the same whole-hour behavior.\n",
